.TH "MEDIADEVICES.GETSUPPORTEDCONSTRAINTS" "3JS" "October 5, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
MediaDevices.getSupportedConstraints \- MediaDevices:
getSupportedConstraints() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]getSupportedConstraints()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]MediaDevices\f[R] interface returns an object whose member fields
each specify one of the constrainable properties the user agent
understands.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
getSupportedConstraints()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
A new object listing the constraints supported by the user agent.
Because only constraints supported by the user agent are included in the
list, each of these Boolean properties has the value \f[CR]true\f[R].
Unsupported constraints are omitted, so reading their properties returns
\f[CR]undefined\f[R].
Available properties are:
.TP
\f[B]aspectRatio\f[R]
The user agent supports constraining the aspect ratio (width divided by
height) of video tracks.
.TP
\f[B]autoGainControl\f[R]
The user agent supports specifying whether automatic gain control is
enabled for audio tracks.
.TP
\f[B]channelCount\f[R]
The user agent supports constraining the number of audio channels, such
as one for mono or two for stereo.
.TP
\f[B]deviceId\f[R]
The user agent supports selecting a media source by its device ID.
.TP
\f[B]displaySurface\f[R]
The user agent supports specifying a preferred display surface type
(browser tab, window, or monitor) for screen capture.
.TP
\f[B]echoCancellation\f[R]
The user agent supports specifying whether echo cancellation is enabled
for audio tracks.
.TP
\f[B]facingMode\f[R]
The user agent supports specifying the direction a camera faces, such as
toward the user or their environment.
.TP
\f[B]frameRate\f[R]
The user agent supports constraining the frame rate of video tracks, in
frames per second.
.TP
\f[B]groupId\f[R]
The user agent supports selecting a media source by its group ID, which
identifies sources belonging to the same physical device.
.TP
\f[B]height\f[R]
The user agent supports constraining the height of video tracks.
.TP
\f[B]latency\f[R]
The user agent supports constraining the latency of audio tracks, in
seconds.
.TP
\f[B]logicalSurface\f[R]
The user agent supports specifying whether screen capture uses logical
display surfaces, which may not be entirely visible onscreen.
.TP
\f[B]noiseSuppression\f[R]
The user agent supports specifying whether noise suppression is enabled
for audio tracks.
.TP
\f[B]resizeMode\f[R]
The user agent supports specifying whether cropping and downscaling can
be used to derive a video track\(cqs resolution and frame rate.
.TP
\f[B]restrictOwnAudio\f[R] \f[I](experimental)\f[R]
The user agent supports specifying whether system audio originating from
the capturing tab is filtered out of screen capture.
.TP
\f[B]sampleRate\f[R]
The user agent supports constraining the sample rate of audio tracks.
.TP
\f[B]sampleSize\f[R]
The user agent supports constraining the sample size of audio tracks, in
bits per linear sample.
.TP
\f[B]suppressLocalAudioPlayback\f[R] \f[I](experimental)\f[R]
The user agent supports specifying whether audio playing in a captured
tab continues to play through the user\(cqs local speakers.
.TP
\f[B]volume\f[R] \f[I](deprecated)\f[R] \f[I](non\-standard)\f[R]
The user agent supports constraining the volume of audio tracks, from
0.0 (silence) to 1.0 (the highest supported volume).
.TP
\f[B]width\f[R]
The user agent supports constraining the width of video tracks.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Checking constraint support
This example generates a table showing whether each of the listed
constraints is supported by your browser.
.SS HTML
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]table\f[R]>
  <\f[B]caption\f[R]>
    Media constraint support
  </\f[B]caption\f[R]>
  <\f[B]thead\f[R]>
    <\f[B]tr\f[R]>
      <\f[B]th\f[R] scope=\(dqcol\(dq>Constraint</\f[B]th\f[R]>
      <\f[B]th\f[R] scope=\(dqcol\(dq>Supported</\f[B]th\f[R]>
    </\f[B]tr\f[R]>
  </\f[B]thead\f[R]>
  <\f[B]tbody\f[R] id=\(dqconstraintSupport\(dq></\f[B]tbody\f[R]>
</\f[B]table\f[R]>
.EE
.SS JavaScript
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] constraints = [
  \(dqaspectRatio\(dq,
  \(dqautoGainControl\(dq,
  \(dqchannelCount\(dq,
  \(dqdeviceId\(dq,
  \(dqdisplaySurface\(dq,
  \(dqechoCancellation\(dq,
  \(dqfacingMode\(dq,
  \(dqframeRate\(dq,
  \(dqgroupId\(dq,
  \(dqheight\(dq,
  \(dqlatency\(dq,
  \(dqlogicalSurface\(dq,
  \(dqnoiseSuppression\(dq,
  \(dqresizeMode\(dq,
  \(dqrestrictOwnAudio\(dq,
  \(dqsampleRate\(dq,
  \(dqsampleSize\(dq,
  \(dqsuppressLocalAudioPlayback\(dq,
  \(dqvolume\(dq,
  \(dqwidth\(dq,
];
\f[B]const\f[R] supportedConstraints = navigator.mediaDevices.getSupportedConstraints();
\f[B]const\f[R] tableBody = document.querySelector(\(dq#constraintSupport\(dq);

\f[B]for\f[R] (\f[B]const\f[R] constraint \f[B]of\f[R] constraints) {
  \f[B]const\f[R] row = document.createElement(\(dqtr\(dq);
  \f[B]const\f[R] name = document.createElement(\(dqth\(dq);
  name.scope = \(dqrow\(dq;
  \f[B]const\f[R] code = document.createElement(\(dqcode\(dq);
  code.textContent = constraint;
  name.appendChild(code);

  \f[B]const\f[R] support = document.createElement(\(dqtd\(dq);
  support.textContent = supportedConstraints[constraint] ? \(dqYes\(dq : \(dqNo\(dq;

  row.append(name, support);
  tableBody.appendChild(row);
}
.EE
.SS Result
.SS Checking constraints before requesting screen capture
The function below sets up the options object for the call to
\f[CR]getDisplayMedia()\f[R].
It adds each of the following constraints only if it is known to be
supported by the browser:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]displaySurface\f[R], requesting a preference for sharing an entire
monitor.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]logicalSurface\f[R], requesting logical display surfaces, which
may not be entirely visible onscreen.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]suppressLocalAudioPlayback\f[R], requesting that captured audio is
not played out of the user\(cqs local speakers.
.PP
These constraints do not limit the display surfaces the user can choose
to share.
Capturing is then started by calling \f[CR]getDisplayMedia()\f[R] and
attaching the returned stream to the \f[CR]<video>\f[R] element
represented by \f[CR]videoElem\f[R].
.IP
.EX
\f[B]async\f[R] \f[B]function\f[R] capture(videoElem) {
  \f[B]const\f[R] supportedConstraints = navigator.mediaDevices.getSupportedConstraints();
  \f[B]const\f[R] displayMediaOptions = {
    video: {},
    audio: {},
  };

  \f[B]if\f[R] (supportedConstraints.displaySurface) {
    displayMediaOptions.video.displaySurface = \(dqmonitor\(dq;
  }

  \f[B]if\f[R] (supportedConstraints.logicalSurface) {
    displayMediaOptions.video.logicalSurface = \f[B]true\f[R];
  }

  \f[B]if\f[R] (supportedConstraints.suppressLocalAudioPlayback) {
    displayMediaOptions.audio.suppressLocalAudioPlayback = \f[B]true\f[R];
  }

  \f[B]try\f[R] {
    videoElem.srcObject =
      \f[B]await\f[R] navigator.mediaDevices.getDisplayMedia(displayMediaOptions);
  } \f[B]catch\f[R] (err) {
    \f[I]/* handle the error */\f[R]
  }
}
.EE
